#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# accounting_form

#% text
# `accounting_form(x)` shows the number `x` with negative values in parentheses and no scientific notation; `accounting_form(x, n)` with `n` significant digits.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The argument is evaluated first; `accounting_form` stays around the value as a display wrapper. The wrapper stays around the value: it is a display directive and changes no computation.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
accounting_form(-1234.5)
#% output
#= accounting_form(-1234.5)

#% cell
accounting_form([1.5, -2.5, 1.0e9])
#% output
#= accounting_form([1.5, -2.5, 1000000000.0])

#% cell
accounting_form(-0.25, 2)
#% output
#= accounting_form(-0.25, 2)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `number_form`, `decimal_form`, `percent_form`
